  "limitations": [
    "Opens .scm and .scx maps through the host-owned blizzard/mpq container alias and reads staredit\\scenario.chk the way the game does: the last section of a name wins, a section past the end of the file keeps the bytes there, negative sizes jump back. A protected map without a listfile is read by the scenario's exact path.",
    "Publishes the scenario's terrain tiles (MTXM) as a map layer; a layer write replaces only the written tiles of MTXM and TILE and the host packs the entry back through blizzard/mpq. With the tileset bound (tileset/*.cv5, vx4ex or vx4, vr4, vf4, wpe from the installation behind the map, its workspace dependency layer) it also publishes the walkable and ground-level minitile layers (read-only) and the terrain as the game draws it, a raster of 32 pixels a tile drawn on demand with levels down to one pixel a tile. The world scene, unit and doodad sprites, unit names (from the game's units.dat and stat_txt.tbl) and triggers are later stages.",
    "Strings are read as UTF-8 when valid, as Remastered does; other strings are decoded with the textEncoding setting (a WHATWG label, default windows-1252) — the map does not record its code page, so it is not guessed."
  ],
